    {
      "id": "BVD-02",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-branching-vector-derivatives",
      "title": "Every complex derivative word appearing in a tensor cofactor has a common bound",
      "hypotheses": "The setting of BVD-01, any vector v₀ in the lowest compact type, an integer cap S and a word of length r≤S in complex matrices of Frobenius norm ≤1.",
      "statement": "The norm of the word applied to v₀ is ≤[8√m(B+S)]^r‖v₀‖. Taking S=m−1 supplies the derivative factors in each of the quantum cofactor minors.",
      "definitions": [
        "The order cap controls each one-step constant, while the actual length controls the power.",
        "For the compact defining example U(4), Λ=(1,0,0,0), the energy on e₄ is 4 and a length-three word has norm 1."
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "BVD-01"
      ],
      "equations": [
