    {
      "id": "BVD-03",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-branching-translated-derivative",
      "title": "The second real derivative of the chosen translated period vector",
      "hypotheses": "For real Lie words take m≥3, a lowest compact-type unit vector, |λa|≤B and opposing-sign gap ≥1000m³. For the period application choose a translate g₀ in the signed unitary group and a smaller-group unit Frobenius direction.",
      "statement": "A real word of length at most m+2 costs the product of (8mB)² times each Frobenius direction norm. On π(g₀)v₀ the indicated second derivative is bounded by [(8mB)²‖g₀‖F²]².",
      "definitions": [
        "Apply the one-place bound with b=√B, so √m b²=√m B.",
        "Conjugate each real direction by g₀⁻¹ and g₀. Invariance of the Frobenius norm under multiplication by signature and adjoint gives ‖g₀⁻¹‖F=‖g₀‖F."
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "DSD-02"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "normalization-branching-translate-second-bound"
      ],
